t.\n   - Do not add or omit items.\n\nContext:\n{context}\n\nQuestion: {question}\n\nAnswer:'} | llm_optimizer[prompt_template_updated]: Document profile: doc_type=unknown, median_chars_per_page=2400, chars_per_section=799 (9599 chars / 12 sections). The document is prose-heavy with argumentative content (e.g., multi-sentence explanations of ANN algorithms, comparisons, and trade-offs), so the regime is PROSE-HEAVY. Prior chunk_size=1000 (~1.25x chars_per_section) improved precision but may still fragment long explanations (e.g., HNSW vs. IVF comparisons). Increasing to 1100 (~1.4x chars_per_section) better captures complete units of reasoning while mitigating precision loss. Overlap=200 (~18%) preserves continuity. Top_k=4 and retriever_type='similarity_score_threshold' with threshold=0.25 balance recall and precision, explicitly prioritizing precision (currently 0.667) without harming recall (currently 1.000). The prompt is further tightened to enforce exhaustive coverage of comparisons, definitions, and multi-step explanations, addressing potential faithfulness and response_relevancy gaps.
